From d04426eca54a3afb20c5f534895744e4056114e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raul Moran <rmg@raulmoranguerra.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:09:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] TimeSourceBase: Split `InnerExecute` into a begin and an
 end half

`InnerExecuteBegin` takes the lock, updates the nearest sync point, latches
the handles and grants them the time interval (or unblocks them);
`InnerExecuteEnd` waits for them, unlatches them, then runs the sync
phase. `InnerExecute` calls one after the other, so nothing changes for
existing time sources: the same steps run in the same order on the same
thread, and in serial execution everything still happens in the second
half.

The split lets a time source start an iteration of another source's
handles and finish it later on the same thread, which a slave time source
running on its master's thread needs (next commits).
